-- title:
--   Uniform bound on I^m-torsion in R/q^mR
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring which is finite as a $\mathbb{Z}$-module (i.e. finitely generated as an abelian group), let $I \subseteq R$ be an ideal, and let $q$ be a prime number whose image $(q : R)$ lies in $I$. The assertion is that there exists a natural number $C$, depending on $R$, $I$ and $q$ but not on $m$, such that for every natural number $m$ the cardinality of the $I^m$-torsion submodule of $R/q^mR$ — that is, of the submodule $\operatorname{torsionBySet}$ of the quotient of $R$ by the principal ideal generated by $(q : R)^m$ consisting of those elements annihilated by every element of the set underlying $I^m$ — satisfies
--   $$\#\bigl((R/q^mR)[I^m]\bigr) \le \#(R/I^m)\cdot q^{C}.$$
--   Both cardinalities are taken as `Nat.card`; since $q \in I$ and $R$ is a finitely generated abelian group, both $R/q^mR$ and $R/I^m$ are finite, so the two sides are genuine natural numbers. The bound is thus a comparison, uniform in $m$ up to a fixed power of $q$, between the $I^m$-torsion of $R/q^mR$ and the order of $R/I^m$.
--
--   This is an abstract Hilbert–Samuel type growth estimate: the $I^m$-torsion of the finite ring $R/q^mR$ grows no faster than the order of $R/I^m$, up to a bounded power of $q$. It is obtained by combining the linear Hilbert–Samuel bounds for $\#(R/I^m)$ in [`Ideal.card_quotient_pow_hilbertSamuel_linear_of_moduleFinite`](thm.html#Ideal.card_quotient_pow_hilbertSamuel_linear_of_moduleFinite) with the duality identities [`CharacterModule.natCard_quotient_ideal_smul_top_eq_natCard_torsionBySet`](thm.html#CharacterModule.natCard_quotient_ideal_smul_top_eq_natCard_torsionBySet) and [`CharacterModule.natCard_eq_of_finite`](thm.html#CharacterModule.natCard_eq_of_finite), and it feeds the growth estimates for torsion in Hecke lattices and in the Néron model of the modular Jacobian used later in the argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Ideal_exists_natCard_torsionBySet_quotient_span_natCast_pow_le_natCard_quotient_pow_mul_pow_of_moduleFinite.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem Ideal.exists_natCard_torsionBySet_quotient_span_natCast_pow_le_natCard_quotient_pow_mul_pow_of_moduleFinite
    (R : Type*) [CommRing R] [Module.Finite ℤ R]
    (I : Ideal R) (q : ℕ) [Fact q.Prime] (hqI : (q : R) ∈ I) :
    ∃ C : ℕ, ∀ m : ℕ,
      Nat.card ↥(Submodule.torsionBySet R (R ⧸ Ideal.span {(q : R) ^ m}) (↑(I ^ m) : Set R)) ≤
        Nat.card (R ⧸ I ^ m) * q ^ C := by sorry
